Q：有哪个瞬间让你觉得这个世界出 bug 了？
@温忘之：蒸米饭的时候，水要距离米一个手指节高。
别管多少水。
也别管手指头多长。
Q：有哪些非常冷门的冷知识？ 
@棠风：咖啡不小心倒在身上，比喝下去更提神。

As the planet warms, one of the clearest direct consequences is more extreme weather—deadly heat waves, floods, hurricanes, wild fires, and maybe even snow storms (though that's a subject of scientific debate). We asked an expert who studies disasters how they prepare. Climate change is making extreme weather events and natural hazards more frequent and intense. Here’s how to prepare before they hit.&nbsp;
Hurricanes, floods, heat waves, and wildfires have become more frequent and severe as the planet warms. The world is seeing unprecedented destruction from this type of weather: the first six months of 2025 marked the U.S.’ costliest first half of a year for major disasters, racking up $101 billion in damages.
Scientists studying extreme weather expect this risk to grow, and…
